    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0822" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg702"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Merry to
                        Acting Secretary of State Loomis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San José, Costa
                                Rica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-05-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1044.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith copy
                    and translation of treaty signed at Managua on April 19 between representatives
                    of Great Britain and Nicaragua relating to the Atlantic coast of the latter,
                    same being intended to definitely settle the old Mosquito question. I have taken
                    the copy from El Diario de la Tarde, semiofficial journal published at Managua,
                    as the official publication may be delayed. You will note that the treaty of
                    Managua, 1860, is abrogated by the first section of the new treaty. * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d715-a1.xml" xpointer="d715-a1"/>
